    {
      "type": "Block",
      "value": "---\nesid: sec-get-error.prototype.stack\ndescription: >\n  An Error instance constructed with a non-Error new.target acquires the\n  [[ErrorData]] internal slot from Error's [[Construct]], so the getter\n  returns a String when invoked directly. Property access via the result\n  does NOT find the inherited accessor, because the result's [[Prototype]]\n  is the new.target's prototype, not Error.prototype.\ninfo: |\n  get Error.prototype.stack\n\n  1. Let E be the this value.\n  2. If E is not an Object, throw a TypeError exception.\n  3. If E does not have an [[ErrorData]] internal slot, return undefined.\n  4. Return an implementation-defined string that represents the stack trace of E.\nincludes: [nativeErrors.js]\nfeatures: [error-stack-accessor, Reflect.construct]\n---",
      "start": 131,
      "end": 901
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " The internal slot is set by Ctor's [[Construct]] regardless of new.target,",
      "start": 1284,
      "end": 1361
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " so the getter (called directly) still produces a string.",
      "start": 1364,
      "end": 1423
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " Property access on the instance does NOT find the inherited accessor:",
      "start": 1507,
      "end": 1579
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " Error.prototype is not on e's prototype chain (it's only on Ctor.prototype,",
      "start": 1582,
      "end": 1660
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " which is bypassed by the foreign new.target). The lookup walks",
      "start": 1663,
      "end": 1728
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " NotAnError.prototype then Object.prototype and returns undefined.",
      "start": 1731,
      "end": 1799
    }
  ],
